  "full_text": "So I was, so I studied control systems and that is the most interesting deviation from optimal control theory that, well, if it's optimal, maybe God chose, I bet God chose a different than optimal controller for the human body. Mr. God, what's the reason you would depart from optimal control theory? Like, I'm sure. There's got to be some reason he would depart from an absolute optimum on purpose. Then said Jeremiah in the day, Thus saith the Lord God of hosts, If thou wilt surely go forth unto the king of Babylon and the princes, then thy soul shall live, and thy city shall not be burned. Oh, look at this. Let's see. Thou shalt not escape out of their hand. If thou wilt not go forth to the king of Babylon, then shall thy city be given into the hand of Chaldeans or Homo's in life, and they shall burn it with fire. Thou shalt not escape out of their hand. So check this out. Let's say you have a fly right here. You go like this. Make your hand go like this. Like this or something. Catch a fly. That's what my brother does. See the flies up? He eats the flies.",
